<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Checklist</h2>

<div id="Sx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="Sx2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all models and algorithms presented, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A clear description of the mathematical setting, assumptions, algorithm, and/or model. [Yes]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An analysis of the properties and complexity (time, space, sample size) of any algorithm. [Yes]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Optional) Anonymized source code, with specification of all dependencies, including external libraries. [Yes]</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any theoretical claim, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Statements of the full set of assumptions of all theoretical results. [Not Applicable] This work is mainly empirical and we make no theoretical claim.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Complete proofs of all theoretical results. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Clear explanations of any assumptions. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all figures and tables that present empirical results, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The code, data, and instructions needed to reproduce the main experimental results (either in the supplemental material or as a URL). [Yes]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All the training details (e.g., data splits, hyperparameters, how they were chosen). [Yes]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A clear definition of the specific measure or statistics and error bars (e.g., with respect to the random seed after running experiments multiple times). [Yes]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A description of the computing infrastructure used. (e.g., type of GPUs, internal cluster, or cloud provider). [Yes]</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If you are using existing assets (e.g., code, data, models) or curating/releasing new assets, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Citations of the creator If your work uses existing assets. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The license information of the assets, if applicable. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">New assets either in the supplemental material or as a URL, if applicable. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Information about consent from data providers/curators. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(e)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Discussion of sensible content if applicable, e.g., personally identifiable information or offensive content. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If you used crowdsourcing or conducted research with human subjects, check if you include:</p>
<ol id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The full text of instructions given to participants and screenshots. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Descriptions of potential participant risks, with links to Institutional Review Board (IRB) approvals if applicable. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I1.i5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The estimated hourly wage paid to participants and the total amount spent on participant compensation. [Not Applicable]</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Probabilistic Interpretation of Losses and Monte-Carlo KFAC</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section explains how the random vector distribution <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{s}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{s}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> used in the main text arises from the probabilistic interpretation of the loss and how it is instantiated in Monte-Carlo KFAC in practice.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>How to implement Monte-Carlo KFAC</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Many supervised learning objectives can be written as negative log-likelihoods. Given an input-target pair <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, let the network output be <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\in\mathbb{R}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\in\mathbb{R}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> that parametrizes a predictive distribution <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math>. This viewpoint covers two standard losses used in practice.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In regression, the loss is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{f}}\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒇</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{f}}\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which corresponds, up to an additive constant, to the negative log-likelihood of the Gaussian model</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{f}})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{y}};{\bm{f}},{\bm{I}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{f}})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{y}};{\bm{f}},{\bm{I}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In multiclass classification, if <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}\in\mathbb{R}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}\in\mathbb{R}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> are logits and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}=\operatorname{softmax}({\bm{f}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}=\operatorname{softmax}({\bm{f}})</annotation></semantics></math>, then the cross-entropy loss is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})=-\log{\bm{p}}_{\bm{y}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})=-\log{\bm{p}}_{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">is the negative log-likelihood of the categorical model</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{f}})=\operatorname{Cat}({\bm{p}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\bm{y}}\mid{\bm{f}})=\operatorname{Cat}({\bm{p}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Given the above probabilistic view of loss functions, we now explain how Monte-Carlo KFAC is implemented. For a training example <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{n},y_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{n},y_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}_{n}={\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{n}),\qquad c_{n}=\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},{\bm{y}}_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}_{n}={\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{n}),\qquad c_{n}=\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},{\bm{y}}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 KFAC: a Layer-wise Curvature Approximation ‣ 3 Method" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we introduced a distribution <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{s}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{s}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">This identity says that the Hessian w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, can be represented as the second moment of a suitable random vector <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In MC-KFAC, this random vector is constructed by sampling a pseudo-target</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\sim q(\cdot\mid{\bm{f}}_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\sim q(\cdot\mid{\bm{f}}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">from the model’s predictive distribution, and then differentiating the corresponding pseudo-loss</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{c}_{n}=-\log q(\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\mid{\bm{f}}_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{c}_{n}=-\log q(\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\mid{\bm{f}}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">The random vector is therefore</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}:=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\tilde{c}_{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}:=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\tilde{c}_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{s}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{s}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution induced by first drawing <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\sim q(\cdot\mid{\bm{f}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\sim q(\cdot\mid{\bm{f}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and then mapping it to the gradient</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}(-\log q(\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\mid{\bm{f}}_{n}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}(-\log q(\tilde{\bm{y}}_{n}\mid{\bm{f}}_{n})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.7" class="ltx_p">With this definition,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}_{n}\sim q(\cdot\mid{\bm{f}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}_{n}\sim q(\cdot\mid{\bm{f}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.8" class="ltx_p">and this expectation equals the output-space GGN term used by KFAC. In practice, we draw <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n,i}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n,i}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n}\approx\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}{\bm{s}}_{n,i}{\bm{s}}_{n,i}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n}\approx\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}{\bm{s}}_{n,i}{\bm{s}}_{n,i}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.9" class="ltx_p">In essence, we applied the following identity:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}_{n}\sim q(\cdot|{\bm{f}}_{n})}[\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(\tilde{y}_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})\cdot\big(\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(\tilde{y}_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})\big)^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}_{n}\sim q(\cdot|{\bm{f}}_{n})}[\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(\tilde{y}_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})\cdot\big(\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(\tilde{y}_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})\big)^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}_{n}\sim q(\cdot|{\bm{f}}_{n})}[\nabla^{2}_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(\tilde{y}_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}_{n}\sim q(\cdot|{\bm{f}}_{n})}[\nabla^{2}_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(\tilde{y}_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla^{2}_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(y_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})=:\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla^{2}_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(y_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})=:\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}c_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.10" class="ltx_p">where the first equality is a familiar consequence of integration by parts while the second equality holds if the Hessian <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(y_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\log q(y_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g., for a simple exponential family where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log q(y_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})=h(y_{n})+T(y_{n})\cdot{\bm{f}}_{n}-A({\bm{f}}_{n})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log q(y_{n}|{\bm{f}}_{n})=h(y_{n})+T(y_{n})\cdot{\bm{f}}_{n}-A({\bm{f}}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now make the distribution <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{s}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{s}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> explicit for two commonly used loss functions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cross-entropy loss.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be the logits for example <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}_{n}=\mathrm{softmax}({\bm{f}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}_{n}=\mathrm{softmax}({\bm{f}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, For a lable <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{n}\in\{1,\cdots,C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{n}\in\{1,\cdots,C\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the softmax cross-entropy loss is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n})=-\log p_{y_{n}}=-{\bm{f}}_{n,y_{n}}+\log\sum_{c=1}^{C}e^{{\bm{f}}_{n,c}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n})=-\log p_{y_{n}}=-{\bm{f}}_{n,y_{n}}+\log\sum_{c=1}^{C}e^{{\bm{f}}_{n,c}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Its Hessian w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n})=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n})=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is the standard output-space GGN term for softmax classification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kunstner et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. To realize this Hessian as a second memoent, we sample a pseudo-target</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}_{n}\sim\operatorname{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}_{n}\sim\operatorname{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and define the corresponding pseudo-loss</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\ell}_{n}=-\log p_{n,\tilde{y}_{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\ell}_{n}=-\log p_{n,\tilde{y}_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the one-hot vector of class <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, then when <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}_{n}=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}_{n}=j</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}:=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\tilde{\ell}_{n}={\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}:=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\tilde{\ell}_{n}={\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{s}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{s}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution induced by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\sim\operatorname{Cat}({\bm{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\sim\operatorname{Cat}({\bm{p}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the map</p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}={\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}={\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Since</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[{\bm{e}}_{j}]={\bm{p}}_{n},\quad\mathbb{E}[{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}]=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[{\bm{e}}_{j}]={\bm{p}}_{n},\quad\mathbb{E}[{\bm{e}}_{j}{\bm{e}}_{j}^{\top}]=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">we obtain that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[{\bm{s}}_{n}]=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[{\bm{s}}_{n}]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\mathbb{E}[({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}]=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\mathbb{E}[({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}]=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, for cross-entropy, the random vector <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by sampling a pseudo-label from the model predictive distribution and differentiating the corresponding pseudo-loss, yielding an unbiased rank-one estimator of the output Hessian.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mean squared error.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For MSE,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{f}}\|^{2},\qquad\nabla_{{\bm{f}}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})={\bm{I}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒇</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{f}}\|^{2},\qquad\nabla_{{\bm{f}}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}},{\bm{y}})={\bm{I}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In this case, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{s}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{s}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> can be taken as a standard Gaussian</p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},{\bm{I}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},{\bm{I}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]={\bm{I}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{s}}_{n}\sim p({\bm{s}}_{n})}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]={\bm{I}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, for MSE, the random vector <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is not obtained by sampling a discrete pseudo-label, but by sampling a Gaussian output perturbation whose covariance matches the output curvature.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Weighted cross-entropy and Fisher</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In data hypercleaning, each training example <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{n},y_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{n},y_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned a learnable nonnegative weight <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the weighted objective</p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\sigma}({\bm{\theta}})=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sigma_{n}\,\ell({\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{n}),y_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\sigma}({\bm{\theta}})=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sigma_{n}\,\ell({\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{n}),y_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For a fixed example <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, define the weighted per-example loss</p>
<table id="A1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{n,\sigma}:=\sigma_{n}\,\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n}),\qquad{\bm{f}}_{n}={\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{n,\sigma}:=\sigma_{n}\,\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n}),\qquad{\bm{f}}_{n}={\bm{f}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, its Hessian with respect to the network output is simply</p>
<table id="A1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell_{n,\sigma}=\sigma_{n}\,\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell_{n,\sigma}=\sigma_{n}\,\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For softmax cross-entropy, let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}=\mathrm{softmax}({\bm{f}}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}=\mathrm{softmax}({\bm{f}}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the Hessian w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n})=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell({\bm{f}}_{n},y_{n})=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and therefore the weighted output-space curvature is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell_{n,\sigma}=\sigma_{n}\bigl(\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell_{n,\sigma}=\sigma_{n}\bigl(\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To realize this matrix as a second moment, we sample a pseudo-label</p>
<table id="A1.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\sim\mathrm{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\sim\mathrm{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and define the vector <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}:=\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}\,({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}:=\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}\,({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the one-hot vector for class <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</p>
<table id="A1.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{j\sim\mathrm{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n})}\big[({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}\big]=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}})-{\bm{p}}{\bm{p}}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{j\sim\mathrm{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n})}\big[({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})^{\top}\big]=\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}})-{\bm{p}}{\bm{p}}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\sigma_{n}\bigl(\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}\bigr)=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell_{n,\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\sigma_{n}\bigl(\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}\bigr)=\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}^{2}\ell_{n,\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, in the weighted setting, the correct Monte-Carlo estimator is obtained by multiplying the usual cross-entropy vector by <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, the corresponding pseudo-loss can be written as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\ell}_{n,\sigma}=\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}\,(-\log p_{n,j}),\qquad j\sim\mathrm{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\ell}_{n,\sigma}=\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}\,(-\log p_{n,j}),\qquad j\sim\mathrm{Cat}({\bm{p}}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">whose gradient with respect to the logits is exactly</p>
<table id="A1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\tilde{\ell}_{n,\sigma}=\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}\,({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{{\bm{f}}_{n}}\tilde{\ell}_{n,\sigma}=\sqrt{\sigma_{n}}\,({\bm{p}}_{n}-{\bm{e}}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">This ensures that the rank-one estimator <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is unbiased for the weighted output Hessian. Scaling the pseudo-loss directly by <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> instead would produce</p>
<table id="A1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\sigma_{n}^{2}\bigl(\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[{\bm{s}}_{n}{\bm{s}}_{n}^{\top}]=\sigma_{n}^{2}\bigl(\operatorname{diag}({\bm{p}}_{n})-{\bm{p}}_{n}{\bm{p}}_{n}^{\top}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">which would over-scale the curvature term.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>More on KFAC</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Originially introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martens and Grosse (2015)</a></cite> for MLP, KFAC has been extended to a range of modern architectures, including convolutional networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grosse and Martens, 2016</a>)</cite>, recurrent networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Martens et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, and transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Eschenhagen et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. There are also refinements of the basic approximation, such as eigenvalue-corrected KFAC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">George et al., 2018</a>, EKFAC)</cite>. KFAC has been successfully applied in the context of optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Osawa et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, model sparsification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, Laplace approximations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daxberger et al., 2021</a>)</cite> and influence functions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grosse et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
We are unaware of works applying this curvature approximation in the context of bilevel optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Meta Learning and KFAC</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Several prior works have incorporated curvature information into meta-learning through KFAC or related approximations, but in fundamentally different ways from ours. We will discuss the difference between our work and theirs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">MAML <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Finn et al., 2017</a>)</cite> is a model-agnostic algorithm to train a model with the greatest sensitivity to the loss function of the new task. Suppose there are tasks obeying <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\sim p(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\sim p(T)</annotation></semantics></math> distribution. We can also formulate MAML as a bilevel optimization problem, if we choose the initialization parameter <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\bm{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{T\sim p(T)}[{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{val}}(\phi_{T}^{*}({\bm{\theta}});T)],\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\phi^{*}_{T}({\bm{\theta}})=\argmin_{\phi}{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{tr}}(\phi;T,{\bm{\theta}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>tr</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\bm{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{T\sim p(T)}[{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{val}}(\phi_{T}^{*}({\bm{\theta}});T)],\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\phi^{*}_{T}({\bm{\theta}})=\argmin_{\phi}{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{tr}}(\phi;T,{\bm{\theta}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the task-adapted model parameter. That is, we want to find the task-specific parameter <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{T}^{*}({\bm{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{T}^{*}({\bm{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math> which will minimize the expected post-adaptation loss across tasks. In practice, MAML does not solve the inner problem to full convergence, but uses one step of SGD from <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> to approximate it, and the objective becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\bm{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{T\sim p(T)}[{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{val}}({\bm{\theta}}-\alpha\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{tr}}({\bm{\theta}};T),T)]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>val</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>tr</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\bm{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{T\sim p(T)}[{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{val}}({\bm{\theta}}-\alpha\nabla_{\bm{\theta}}{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{tr}}({\bm{\theta}};T),T)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">for the learning rate <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. There are several works that have adapted KFAC to improve the algorithms for MAML. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2023)</a></cite> replace the inner optimizer with natural gradient descent preconditioned by KFAC, focusing on improving convergence speed rather than on BO. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grant et al. (2018)</a></cite> reinterpret MAML as hierarchical Bayes and employ KFAC only to approximate Hessian determinants within Laplace correction to the marginal likelihood, rather than to compute hypergradients. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2023)</a></cite> propose BM-KFP, which applies Kronecker factorization to the parameter of a learned meta-optimizer, a structural efficiency technique unrelated to Hessian approximation. Meta-Curvature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park and Oliva, 2019</a>)</cite> learns gradient transformation matrices for fast adaptation, and to ensure tractability, parameterizes them with low-rank and Kronecker-structured factors, which are conceptually related to KFAC’s block-Kronecker approximation of curvature. Unlike KFAC, however, these operators are not derived from the GGN but are meta-learned directly from data. In contrast, we use KFAC as an efficient means for inverse Hessian-vector products.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Connection between GU and IFT</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The idea of MAML can be seen as a one-step gradient unrolling (GU), and we can show that GU is equivalent to IFT for the one-step case or the infinite step case. We consider the BO formulation:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\bm{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}}\;\Phi(\bm{\lambda}):=\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}\bigl(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}(\bm{\lambda})\bigr),\quad\text{s.t.}\quad{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}(\bm{\lambda})=\arg\min_{{\bm{\theta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\bm{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}}\;\Phi(\bm{\lambda}):=\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}\bigl(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}(\bm{\lambda})\bigr),\quad\text{s.t.}\quad{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}(\bm{\lambda})=\arg\min_{{\bm{\theta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, we demonstrate how to solve it using GU and how this is connected to the hypergradient. Let the inner problem be optimized by <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps of gradient descent with step size <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{t+1}\;=\;{\bm{\theta}}^{t}-\eta\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t}),\qquad t=0,\dots,T-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{t+1}\;=\;{\bm{\theta}}^{t}-\eta\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t}),\qquad t=0,\dots,T-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with initialization <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (typically independent of <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>). Define the unrolled outer objective
<math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{T}(\bm{\lambda}):=\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},\theta^{T}(\bm{\lambda}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{T}(\bm{\lambda}):=\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},\theta^{T}(\bm{\lambda}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the chain rule,</p>
<table id="A3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi_{T}(\bm{\lambda})\;=\;\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T})\;+\;\bigl(\tfrac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{\theta}}^{T}}{\mathrm{d}\bm{\lambda}}\bigr)^{\top}\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi_{T}(\bm{\lambda})\;=\;\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T})\;+\;\bigl(\tfrac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{\theta}}^{T}}{\mathrm{d}\bm{\lambda}}\bigr)^{\top}\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}^{t}:=\tfrac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{\theta}}^{t}}{\mathrm{d}\bm{\lambda}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}^{t}:=\tfrac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{\theta}}^{t}}{\mathrm{d}\bm{\lambda}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{H}}_{t}\coloneqq\nabla_{22}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mn>22</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{H}}_{t}\coloneqq\nabla_{22}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}^{0}=\frac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{\theta}}^{0}}{\mathrm{d}\bm{\lambda}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}^{0}=\frac{\mathrm{d}{\bm{\theta}}^{0}}{\mathrm{d}\bm{\lambda}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>), differentiating the update in <a href="#A3.E6" title="In Appendix C Connection between GU and IFT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and expanding the recursion, we can get the explicit formula for <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{S}}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{S}}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{S}}^{t}-\eta\Bigl[\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})\;+\;\nabla_{22}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})\,{\bm{S}}^{t}\Bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mn>22</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{S}}^{t}-\eta\Bigl[\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})\;+\;\nabla_{22}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})\,{\bm{S}}^{t}\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})+({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t}){\bm{S}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})+({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t}){\bm{S}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})+({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t})\big(({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t-1}){\bm{S}}^{t-1}-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t-1})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})+({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t})\big(({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t-1}){\bm{S}}^{t-1}-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t-1})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})-\eta({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t})\nabla_{21}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t-1})+\big(\prod_{j=t-1}^{t}({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j})\big){\bm{S}}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})-\eta({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t})\nabla_{21}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t-1})+\big(\prod_{j=t-1}^{t}({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j})\big){\bm{S}}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\,\sum_{s=0}^{t}\Biggl(\;\prod_{j=s+1}^{t}\bigl({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j}\bigr)\Biggr)\,\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{s})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.337em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\,\sum_{s=0}^{t}\Biggl(\;\prod_{j=s+1}^{t}\bigl({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j}\bigr)\Biggr)\,\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Plugging back to equation <a href="#A3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Appendix C Connection between GU and IFT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, the <math id="A3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-step unrolled hypergradient is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi_{T}(\bm{\lambda})=\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T})\;-\;\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Bigl[\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})^{\top}\,\Bigl(\prod_{j=t+1}^{T-1}\bigl({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j}\bigr)\Bigr)\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T})\Bigr],\;}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi_{T}(\bm{\lambda})=\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T})\;-\;\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Bigl[\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})^{\top}\,\Bigl(\prod_{j=t+1}^{T-1}\bigl({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j}\bigr)\Bigr)\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{T})\Bigr],\;}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where products over an empty index set are the identity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, recall the expression of IFT based hypergradient:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi(\bm{\lambda})=\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\;-\;\nabla_{12}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\bigl({\bm{H}}\bigr)^{-1}\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}),}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝑯</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi(\bm{\lambda})=\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\;-\;\nabla_{12}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\bigl({\bm{H}}\bigr)^{-1}\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}),}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the inner problem and <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{H}}=\nabla_{22}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mn>22</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{H}}=\nabla_{22}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, and this value is usually estimated by running a few steps of an optimization algorithm. For <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}^{1}=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}^{1}=-\eta\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</p>
<table id="A3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;\nabla_{\lambda}\Phi_{1}(\bm{\lambda})=\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{1})\;-\;\eta\,\bigl[\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{0})\bigr]^{\top}\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;\nabla_{\lambda}\Phi_{1}(\bm{\lambda})=\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{1})\;-\;\eta\,\bigl[\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{0})\bigr]^{\top}\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Comparing to the IFT form, if we (i) approximate <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{*}\approx{\bm{\theta}}^{0}\approx{\bm{\theta}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{*}\approx{\bm{\theta}}^{0}\approx{\bm{\theta}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and (ii) approximate the inner curvature by the identity,
<math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{H}}\approx{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>≈</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{H}}\approx{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{H}}^{-1}\nabla_{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}\approx\nabla_{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{H}}^{-1}\nabla_{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}\approx\nabla_{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>),
then with <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math> we recover the same algebraic structure:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi(\bm{\lambda})\;\approx\;\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\;-\;\nabla_{12}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\bm{\lambda}}\Phi(\bm{\lambda})\;\approx\;\nabla_{1}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\;-\;\nabla_{12}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star})\,\nabla_{2}\,\mathcal{J}_{\text{out}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{\star}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lorraine et al. (2020)</a></cite> shows that as <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, under the assumption <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}^{0}={\bm{\theta}}^{1}=\dots={\bm{\theta}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}^{0}={\bm{\theta}}^{1}=\dots={\bm{\theta}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is contractive, GU can again happen to align with IFT. To see this, consider <math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}{\bm{S}}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}{\bm{S}}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\prod_{j=t+1}^{T-1}({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j})\big)\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\big(\prod_{j=t+1}^{T-1}({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}_{j})\big)\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{t})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big(\prod_{j=t+1}^{T-1}({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}})\Big)\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})\Big]\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>𝑯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big(\prod_{j=t+1}^{T-1}({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}})\Big)\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})\Big]\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{\theta}}^{0}={\bm{\theta}}^{*}={\bm{\theta}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{\theta}}^{0}={\bm{\theta}}^{*}={\bm{\theta}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}\Big)^{T-1-t}\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>𝑯</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}\Big)^{T-1-t}\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}\Big)^{t}\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>𝑯</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\Big[-\eta\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big({\bm{I}}-\eta{\bm{H}}\Big)^{t}\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex70.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">re-index</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-{\bm{H}}^{-1}\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-{\bm{H}}^{-1}\nabla_{21}^{2}\mathcal{J}_{\text{in}}(\bm{\lambda},{\bm{\theta}}^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex71.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Neumann series and contractive</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Plugging back to equation <a href="#A3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Appendix C Connection between GU and IFT" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we will get the same expression as the hypergradient. Therefore, under the local optimality and contraction assumption, unrolling to infinity is exactly implicit differentiation: the Neumann series induced by unrolling sums to the inverse Hessian, turning GU into IFT. Our KFAC-based hypergradient can be seen as a middle ground between <math id="A3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, balancing the hypergradient accuracy and the computational cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>BERT Data Hypercleaning</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional experimental details and results for the BERT data hypercleaning experiments described in the main text. The bilevel formulation is the same as in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Data Hypercleaning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, with the difference that the inner model is a pretrained BERT classifier and we vary the number of trainable layers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider text classification tasks from the WRENCH benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, namely <span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SemEval</span>, <span id="A4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Youtube</span>, and <span id="A4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Trec</span>. These datasets are weak-supervision benchmarks with noisy labeling sources and are large enough to show clear performance differences between bilevel optimization methods while remaining computationally manageable for repeated BERT fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use the pretrained BERT-base model (110M parameters) from <span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HuggingFace</span>. In the inner problem, we optimize with AdamW using a fixed learning rate of <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> and a cosine learning-rate scheduler. In the outer problem, we use SGD with momentum <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math> and perform a grid search over learning rates <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.01,0.1,1,10,100\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.01,0.1,1,10,100\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each outer iteration contains 10 inner updates. For KFAC and KFAC EMP, we use damping <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>; for CG, we use 3 conjugate-gradient iterations; for Neumann, we use either 3 or 10 truncation steps; and for SAMA, we set <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. All experiments use batch size 128 and maximum sequence length 100. We run each experiment for 2000 iterations and report averages over multiple random seeds on a single NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPU. Full numerical results are shown in <a href="#A4.T7" title="In Appendix D BERT Data Hypercleaning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Comparison of Methods on <span id="A4.T7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Trec</span>, <span id="A4.T7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SemEval</span>, and <span id="A4.T7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Youtube</span> at Different Tuning Levels. Each entry shows Accuracy and Training Time. Each result is averaged over 5 runs. These are the same results as <a href="#S5.F4" title="In 5 Curvature Matters at Scale" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> but in numbers. </figcaption>
